      "question": "<figure class=\"practice-figure\" style=\"max-width:70mm;margin:2mm auto\"><img src=\"resources/exams/edexcel-9ma0-01-2018-june/q03-figure.svg\" alt=\"Sector AOB of a circle with centre O: two radii of length r cm, OA and OB, with the angle theta at O between them and the arc AB.\"></figure><p>Figure 1 shows a sector <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"AOB\"></span> of a circle with centre <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"O\"></span> and radius <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r\\,\\mathrm{cm}\"></span>.</p><p>The angle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"AOB\"></span> is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\theta\"></span> radians.<br>The area of the sector <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"AOB\"></span> is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"11\\,\\mathrm{cm}^2\"></span></p><p>Given that the perimeter of the sector is 4 times the length of the arc <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"AB\"></span>, find the exact value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r\"></span>. <span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></p>",
