    {
      "id": "exam/edexcel-9ma0-01-2018-june/q4",
      "question": "<p>The curve with equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=2\\ln(8-x)\"></span> meets the line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=x\"></span> at a single point, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=\\alpha\"></span>.</p><ol class=\"parts\"><li>Show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"3&lt;\\alpha&lt;4\"></span> <span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li></ol><figure class=\"practice-figure\" style=\"max-width:110mm;margin:2mm auto\"><img src=\"resources/exams/edexcel-9ma0-01-2018-june/q04-figure.svg\" alt=\"Graph of y = 2 ln(8 - x), decreasing from the upper left, crossing the y-axis just above 4 and the x-axis to the right of x = 4, and the line y = x through O; they cross between x = 3 and x = 4. The values 4 are marked on both axes.\"></figure><p>Figure 2 shows the graph of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=2\\ln(8-x)\"></span> and the graph of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=x\"></span>.</p><p>A student uses the iteration formula</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x_{n+1}=2\\ln(8-x_n),\\qquad n\\in\\mathbb N\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>in an attempt to find an approximation for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\alpha\"></span>.</p><p>Using the graph and starting with <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_1=4\"></span></p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"2\"><li>determine whether or not this iteration formula can be used to find an approximation for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\alpha\"></span>, justifying your answer. <span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li></ol>",
      "steps": [
