      "id": "exam/edexcel-9ma0-01-2018-june/q5",
      "question": "<p>Given that</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=\\frac{3\\sin\\theta}{2\\sin\\theta+2\\cos\\theta}\\qquad -\\frac{\\pi}{4}&lt;\\theta&lt;\\frac{3\\pi}{4}\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>show that</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{\\mathrm dy}{\\mathrm d\\theta}=\\frac{A}{1+\\sin 2\\theta}\\qquad -\\frac{\\pi}{4}&lt;\\theta&lt;\\frac{3\\pi}{4}\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span> is a rational constant to be found. <span class=\"marks\">(5)</span></p>",
