    {
      "id": "exam/edexcel-9ma0-01-2018-june/q6",
      "question": "<figure class=\"practice-figure\" style=\"max-width:85mm;margin:2mm auto\"><img src=\"resources/exams/edexcel-9ma0-01-2018-june/q06-figure.svg\" alt=\"Not to scale. Axes with origin O; a circle C with centre A in the first quadrant; the line l crosses the axes near O and touches C at P on its upper left side.\"></figure><p>The circle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span> has centre <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span> with coordinates <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(7,5)\"></span>.</p><p>The line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l\"></span>, with equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=2x+1\"></span>, is the tangent to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span> at the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\"></span>, as shown in Figure 3.</p><ol class=\"parts\"><li>Show that an equation of the line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"PA\"></span> is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2y+x=17\"></span> <span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></li><li>Find an equation for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span>. <span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></li></ol><p>The line with equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=2x+k,\\quad k\\ne 1\"></span> is also a tangent to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span>.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"3\"><li>Find the value of the constant <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\"></span>. <span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></li></ol>",
