    {
      "id": "exam/edexcel-9ma0-01-2018-june/q10",
      "question": "<p>The height above ground, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"H\"></span> metres, of a passenger on a roller coaster can be modelled by the differential equation</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{\\mathrm dH}{\\mathrm dt}=\\frac{H\\cos(0.25t)}{40}\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\"></span> is the time, in seconds, from the start of the ride.</p><p>Given that the passenger is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"5\\,\\mathrm m\"></span> above the ground at the start of the ride,</p><ol class=\"parts\"><li>show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"H=5\\mathrm e^{0.1\\sin(0.25t)}\"></span> <span class=\"marks\">(5)</span></li><li>State the maximum height of the passenger above the ground. <span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></li></ol><p>The passenger reaches the maximum height, for the second time, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T\"></span> seconds after the start of the ride.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"3\"><li>Find the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T\"></span>. <span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li></ol>",
