      "id": "exam/edexcel-9ma0-01-2018-june/q12",
      "question": "<p>The value, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\pounds V\"></span>, of a vintage car <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\"></span> years after it was first valued on 1st January 2001, is modelled by the equation</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"V=Ap^t\\qquad\\text{where }A\\text{ and }p\\text{ are constants}\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>Given that the value of the car was £32&#8239;000 on 1st January 2005 and £50&#8239;000 on 1st January 2012</p><ol class=\"parts\"><li><ol class=\"parts\" type=\"i\"><li>find <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\"></span> to 4 decimal places,</li><li>show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span> is approximately 24&#8239;800</li></ol><span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></li><li>With reference to the model, interpret<ol class=\"parts\" type=\"i\"><li>the value of the constant <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span>,</li><li>the value of the constant <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\"></span>.</li></ol><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li></ol><p>Using the model,</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"3\"><li>find the year during which the value of the car first exceeds £100&#8239;000 <span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></li></ol>",
